I think the HCLs are the definitive (externally accessible :-) source.

We've tended to stick with controller families (so that updating a
driver was all that was needed) rather than introducing completely new
ones.  Recent additions have been Adaptec (but not all of them), Intel
EEPro100 NIC, NCR/Symbios 896, and a couple of recent Mylex RAID
controllers. Those are only the ones I know of, ie there may be
others.

